MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

During the pay-gate-loop refresh commit (0023050) git rejected the
tree build with 'invalid object … for docs/DASH_IAI_ONE_RUNTIME_APP_SPEC.md'.
The blob was missing from .git/objects/8a/ but the working-tree file
was intact, so hash-object -w restored it. Subsequent investigation:

- git gc --auto from Xcode's libexec git was stuck (PID 22721, 0.01s
  CPU over 12 min wall) — killed.
- git fsck --full --strict and --connectivity-only both hang silently.
  HEAD itself + 10 ancestors resolve cheaply, so corruption is local
  to specific deep-tree walks rather than wholesale.
- macOS Finder/iCloud has produced .git/index 2, .git/index 3 — a
  known precursor to object-DB damage on macOS.
- Object DB is loose-only (.git/objects/pack empty, 7.5 MiB total).

Recommended recovery: re-clone from origin, fsck the fresh copy,
cherry-pick the 8 local-only commits (all listed in the doc and
verified cat-file-reachable). Hold off on push until repaired.

Until that is done: keep working in the dirty worktree (commits
succeed because each commit is internally consistent), but no push,
no gc --aggressive, no .git/objects/ rewrites.
